151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nHow many units apart is any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with side of 6 units? Express your answer in simplest radical form.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b0c864f27287856360fda3e11656a529cc49721449efde5d17ce3ded82e3d3d5"},"seconds":24.0297110080719,"seed":61437116914012972,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem of finding how many units apart any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with a side length of 6 units are, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the Structure of a Regular Hexagon**:\n   - A regular hexagon is a six-sided polygon where all sides are equal in length, and all internal angles are equal.\n   - Each internal angle in a regular hexagon is \\(120^\\circ\\).\n   - A regular hexagon can be divided into 6 equilateral triangles.\n\n2. **Relate Side Length to the Height of Equilateral Triangles**:\n   - Each side of the hexagon is 6 units.\n   - The height of an equilateral triangle with side length \\(s\\) can be found using the formula for the height of an equilateral triangle: \\(h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times s\\).\n   - For our hexagon, \\(s = 6\\), so the height of each equilateral triangle is:\n     \\[\n     h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 6 = 3\\sqrt{3}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Determine the Distance Between Parallel Sides**:\n   - In a regular hexagon, the distance between any pair of parallel sides is twice the height of one of the equilateral triangles (since the hexagon can be divided into two sets of three equilateral triangles each, stacked on top of each other).\n   - Therefore, the distance between parallel sides is:\n     \\[\n     2 \\times 3\\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer**:\n   - The distance between any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with a side length of 6 units is:\n     \\[\n     \\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}\n     \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
